# Honoured by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages (other hosts: set the same headers in their settings).
# On hosts that ignore this file it is simply served as plain text, so it must never name the
# sign-in folder. The sign-in page carries its own robots meta tag instead.
# There is also deliberately no robots.txt: a "Disallow" line would publish the sign-in path
# and stop crawlers from ever seeing the noindex rules.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
